These are the Cyrillic fonts created by Nana Glonti and Alexander Samarinat the Institute for High Energy Physics, Protvino, USSR.Email: SAMARIN@VXCERN.DECNET.CERN.CHThe fonts were completed and released in 1989.---------------------------- list of files -------------------cmcbx10.mfcmcbxsl10.mfcmcbxti10.mfcmcitt10.mfcmcsl10.mfcmcss10.mfcmcssdc10.mfcmcti10.mfcmctt10.mfcmcyr10.mfcyrillic.mf        - steer file + kerning tablecitall.mf          - lower case italic letterscyrl.mf            - lower case letterscyru.mf            - upper case letterscytextit.mf        - steer file for italicThe following Computer Modern character files must also be available to METAFONT at the time of compilation.For the ``Roman'' styles---romand.mf	  % numeralsromanp.mf	  % ampersand, question marks, currency signFor the ``Italic'' styles---itald.mf	  % numeralsitalp.mf	  % ampersand, question marks, currency signFor both styles---punct.mf	  % punctuation symbols common to roman and italic textcomlig.mf	  %  simple ligatures